cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived release."
title: "QSafety QAE: Quantum amplitude estimation tools for safety probability models"
type: software
version: 0.1.3
date-released: 2026-10-09
abstract: >-
  Independently authored tools for comparing classical Monte Carlo and ideal
  maximum-likelihood quantum amplitude estimation in safety and reliability
  probability models. The repository also contains selected uncertainty,
  strong-classical-baseline, schedule, and finite-table oracle research scripts.
  This is a code-only software archive, not a complete manuscript data archive
  or a claim of end-to-end quantum advantage. The PyPI wheel provides the core
  qsafety library; research scripts are available from the tagged repository.
keywords:
  - process safety
  - quantitative risk assessment
  - reliability
  - rare-event probability
  - quantum amplitude estimation
authors:
  - family-names: "Lee"
    given-names: "Ugwiyeon"
    affiliation: "Korea Gas Safety Corporation"
    email: "lyullee@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-8976-5363"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lyullee/qsafety-qae"
license: MIT
